      "id": "claim_8f3b21b6773146f98ed2b9911f4a2aec",
      "statement": "The harness separates two axes at intake: Lane (tiny | normal | high-risk) drives ceremony/proof, while Confidence (high | medium | low) drives interruption; ceremony scales with risk and the human gate scales with ambiguity, and agents never ask a human to classify risk.",
